/* book Worked example 2: Q: A link must carry 9600 bit/s with a raised cosine of α = 0.25. Compare binary PAM and Gray-coded 4-PAM: symbol rate, bandwidth, thresholds, Pe at Eb/N₀ = 10 dB, and the Eb/N₀ for Pe = 10⁻⁵.
   1. Binary: Rs = 9600 baud, B = 4800 × 1.25 = 6000 Hz, one threshold. 4-PAM: Rs = 4800 baud, B = 2400 × 1.25 = 3000 Hz, three thresholds (0 and ±2d).
   2. At 10 dB, binary: Pe = Q(√20) = 3.87 × 10⁻⁶.
   3. 4-PAM: Es/N₀ = 2 × 10 = 20; argument √(6 × 20/15) = √8 = 2.828; Pe = 1.5 × Q(2.828) = 1.5 × 2.34 × 10⁻³ = 3.51 × 10⁻³, BER ≈ 1.75 × 10⁻³.
   4. For 10⁻⁵: binary 9.59 dB; 4-PAM solves 1.5 Q(x) = 10⁻⁵, x = 4.355, Eb/N₀ = x² × 15/12 = 23.7, that is 13.75 dB.
   Answer: Binary: 9600 baud, 6000 Hz, 1 threshold, Pe = 3.87 × 10⁻⁶ at 10 dB, needs 9.59 dB. 4-PAM: 4800 baud, 3000 Hz, 3 thresholds, Pe = 3.51 × 10⁻³ at 10 dB, needs 13.75 dB. Half the bandwidth costs about 4.2 dB. */
